      "versionNonce": 227,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Project Activities & Solutions",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Project Activities & Solutions",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "p2_ms_body",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 752,
      "y": 2758,
      "width": 656,
      "height": 174,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 228,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 229,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Lāwa'i Solar Project was World's Largest Solar Storage Peaker project at the time.\nAtlas began installing the multimode SCADA communications systems, Energy Control\nNetwork and Single mode Telco system in 2018. We furnished and installed all new fiber\noptic cable terminations and copper communications, certifying and installing new panels\nswitches and PoE media converters throughout the existing site, to over 30 locations,\nall while the plant operations were running. The majority of the work was completed in\n2019 however, we were mobilized as new locations were added and reconfigurations of the\nPoE Panels and SCADA systems were required to complete a design and installation for the\nOperations and Maintenance building. After the project, AES asked Atlas to design the\nPoE panels for the next projects and to develop a standard for the O&M building as well.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Lāwa'i Solar Project was World's Largest Solar Storage Peaker project at the time.\nAtlas began installing the multimode SCADA communications systems, Energy Control\nNetwork and Single mode Telco system in 2018. We furnished and installed all new fiber\noptic cable terminations and copper communications, certifying and installing new panels\nswitches and PoE media converters throughout the existing site, to over 30 locations,\nall while the plant operations were running. The majority of the work was completed in\n2019 however, we were mobilized as new locations were added and reconfigurations of the\nPoE Panels and SCADA systems were required to complete a design and installation for the\nOperations and Maintenance building. After the project, AES asked Atlas to design the\nPoE panels for the next projects and to develop a standard for the O&M building as well.",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
